{"kind":"article","seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"Related Documentation","identifiers":["doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/GettingStartedWithSwiftUI","doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/GettingStartedWithUIKit","doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/Accessibility"],"anchor":"Related-Documentation"}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"text":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The default Empty\/Loading\/Error placeholders’ text — “Nothing Here,” “Loading,” “Retry,” “Something Went Wrong,” “Connection Issue” — comes from a String Catalog, "},{"code":"Resources\/Localizable.xcstrings","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", resolved from ScreenStates’ own bundle ("},{"code":"Bundle.module","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":") rather than your app’s. That’s deliberate: a custom title your app passes in (see below) is never run back through localization, and a language you add to "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"your own"}]},{"type":"text","text":" app’s catalog has no effect on these five strings — they only ever resolve against ScreenStates’ bundle. English, Spanish, French, and Russian are built in today."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Adding-a-language-to-ScreenStates","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Adding a language to ScreenStates"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This is a change to the package itself, not something a consuming app can do on its own — it needs a PR. Open "},{"code":"Resources\/Localizable.xcstrings","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and add a "},{"code":"localizations","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" entry for the new language code under each of the five string keys:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["\"Retry\" : {","  \"comment\" : \"Title of the button that retries loading after an error.\",","  \"localizations\" : {","    \"en\" : { \"stringUnit\" : { \"state\" : \"translated\", \"value\" : \"Retry\" } },","    \"de\" : { \"stringUnit\" : { \"state\" : \"translated\", \"value\" : \"Wiederholen\" } }","  }","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"json"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Every one of the five keys needs an entry for every language — a string present in English but missing a translation elsewhere fails CI (see below). "},{"code":"ScreenStatesStrings.swift","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"‘s doc comments list all five keys and their English text if you’re starting from scratch."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Overriding-text-per-app","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overriding text per-app"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"You don’t need a new language, or a PR, to show different text than the built-in default — two options, depending on how much you want to replace:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ScreenStateDefaultEmptyView(title:)"},{"text":" takes a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"title"},{"text":" directly, bypassing ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Localizable.xcstrings"},{"text":" entirely for that one string. Pass your own localized string (from your own app’s String Catalog, ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NSLocalizedString"},{"text":", whatever) instead of the default:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["ScreenStateDefaultEmptyView(title: String(localized: \"No Results\"))"]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ScreenStateDefaultErrorView"},{"text":" has no equivalent for its title or Retry button text today — only the error’s own message is customizable, via ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateDisplayableError","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"For anything else — the Error placeholder’s title, the Retry button’s text, or any text at all in a shape the built-in views don’t expose a parameter for — pass a fully custom placeholder instead of the default one, via ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateView","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":"’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"empty"},{"text":"\/","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"loading"},{"text":"\/","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"error"},{"text":" builder closures (see ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/GettingStartedWithSwiftUI","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":"\/","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/GettingStartedWithUIKit","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":") or ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateViewController","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":"‘s equivalent. A custom placeholder can still reuse ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenState\/accessibilityAnnouncement","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" so VoiceOver announces transitions with the same wording your custom text uses, instead of the default’s.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]}],"kind":"content"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates"]]},"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"ScreenStates"}],"role":"article","title":"Localization","roleHeading":"Article"},"sections":[],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/Localization","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/screenstates\/localization"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"abstract":[{"text":"How the default placeholders’ built-in text is localized, how to add a language, and how to show different text instead without touching ScreenStates itself.","type":"text"}],"references":{"doc://screenstates.ScreenStates/documentation/ScreenStates/Accessibility":{"type":"topic","role":"article","kind":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Everything the default placeholders — and your own custom ones — get for free: VoiceOver, Reduce Motion, Increase Contrast, Dynamic Type, and stable identifiers for XCUITest."}],"url":"\/documentation\/screenstates\/accessibility","title":"Accessibility","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/Accessibility"},"doc://screenstates.ScreenStates/documentation/ScreenStates/ScreenStateContainerView":{"type":"topic","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"ScreenStateContainerView"}],"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/screenstates\/screenstatecontainerview","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A "},{"code":"UIView","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" that swaps its content for the right placeholder based on a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenState","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", mirroring "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateView","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" from the SwiftUI side."}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"ScreenStateContainerView"}],"title":"ScreenStateContainerView","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateContainerView"},"doc://screenstates.ScreenStates/documentation/ScreenStates/ScreenState/accessibilityAnnouncement":{"type":"topic","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"accessibilityAnnouncement","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","text":"String","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"The same text the default placeholders announce to VoiceOver for","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"this case, reusable by a fully custom placeholder that wants to","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"announce transitions with the same wording instead of inventing its","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"own. ","type":"text"},{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" for ","type":"text"},{"code":".data","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", since at that point a custom placeholder’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"own content is what VoiceOver should read, not a transition","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"announcement.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/screenstates\/screenstate\/accessibilityannouncement","title":"accessibilityAnnouncement","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenState\/accessibilityAnnouncement"},"doc://screenstates.ScreenStates/documentation/ScreenStates":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates","kind":"symbol","role":"collection","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/screenstates","title":"ScreenStates","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Give any screen a standard "},{"code":"Empty","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" \/ "},{"code":"Loading","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" \/ "},{"code":"Data","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" \/ "},{"code":"Error","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" state, usable from both UIKit and SwiftUI."}]},"doc://screenstates.ScreenStates/documentation/ScreenStates/ScreenStateViewController":{"type":"topic","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"